    "problem_statement": "When an LwM2M SENML CBOR read of a resource instance is serialized as a time series (cached values), the emitted CBOR record is missing the resource-instance name. The name entry produced for a resource instance whose instance id is 0 is just the resource name (e.g. \"10\") instead of the full resource-instance name (e.g. \"10/0\"). The encoded payload must carry the complete resource-instance name \"10/0\" for every time-serialized record, matching what is produced for resources, so that a compliant SENML CBOR decoder can reconstruct the correct path.",
